{"availability":"available","full":"winebarrel/pistachio","name":"pistachio","description":"pistachio is a declarative schema management tool for PostgreSQL with a Terraform-like plan/apply workflow.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Go","stars":58,"forks":1,"created":"2026-02-21T01:22:56Z","updated":"2026-10-06T15:39:42Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://winebarrel.github.io/pistachio/","topics":["cli","database-migration","database-migrations","db-migration","ddl","declarative","declarative-migrations","golang","postgres","postgresql","schema-management","schema-migration","schema-migrations"],"demo":"https://pistachio-demo.winebarrel.workers.dev/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T15:43:23.500Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T15:43:23.500Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T15:43:23.500Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T08:15:58.621Z","stars":58,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-06T15:43:23.500Z","stars":58,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["pistachio is a declarative schema management tool for PostgreSQL with a Terraform-like plan/apply workflow. You write the schema you want as DDL in SQL files. pistachio compares the database with the files and prints the DDL that makes the database match.","pista plan prints that DDL. pista apply runs it. pista dump writes the files from an existing database.","The playground runs pista diff on two schemas that you edit in the page. There is nothing to install."],"features":["An object removed from the file is dropped only when --allow-drop includes its type. Until then, the plan shows the drop as a -- skipped: comment. See Controlling drops.","-- pista:renamed-from oldname above an object changes a drop and a create into a RENAME. See Renaming objects.","apply --with-tx runs the plan in one transaction. -- pista:concurrently marks an index for CONCURRENTLY, which cannot run in a transaction. --try-tx handles both cases. See Transactions and locks.","plan --explain reports which statements scan or rewrite a table, what they block, and how big the table is. See Explaining a plan.","plan --out writes a plan file. apply-from runs it later, and refuses to run if the database changed in between. See Plan files."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/winebarrel/pistachio/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"6a3e7efeb81eb79f321e2f8c8fb3f283ef3178a2e7992c22ef2fc56bd5a085d3","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T17:56:53.794Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T17:56:53.794Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"pistachio is a declarative schema management tool for PostgreSQL with a Terraform-like plan/apply workflow. You write the schema you want as DDL in SQL files. pistachio compares the database with the files and prints the DDL that makes the database match.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/winebarrel/pistachio/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"6a3e7efeb81eb79f321e2f8c8fb3f283ef3178a2e7992c22ef2fc56bd5a085d3","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/winebarrel/pistachio/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T17:56:53.795Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-06T15:39:42Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/winebarrel/pistachio/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T17:56:53.795Z","hash":"6a3e7efeb81eb79f321e2f8c8fb3f283ef3178a2e7992c22ef2fc56bd5a085d3","originalBytes":5747,"storedBytes":5747,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["plan","pista","see","pistachio","schema","files","run","schema.sql","sql","apply","file","postgresql","runs","table","bash","column","create","database","ddl","object","prints","add","database.","drop","dump","email","every","files.","index","management","objects","there","winebarrel","writes","allow-drop","alter","becomes","changed","changes","commands","composite","concurrently","diff","docker","domains","dropped","edit","getting","history","host","how","includes","install","mise","mydb","nothing","one","o